IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 12, SECTIONS 95 TO 96A (employee records, the written
-- record of key employment terms, pay slips, retrenchment information).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Seams S9, S10, S11 and S12 (PLAN.md section 4) are ANSWERED here:
--       S9  `s 95(1) the employer failed to comply`    S10 `s 95A(2) the employer failed to comply`
--       S11 `s 96(1) the employer failed to comply`    S12 `s 96A the employer failed to comply with a requirement in the notification`
--     each MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE where the Act says the employer failed, NOTHING otherwise.  The Act has no sentence
--     that says an employer who did everything has complied, so no FALSE is given (NOTES.md, Reading a result).
--   * The Interpretation Act module (sgia-interpretation-time, copied unchanged) counts the 14 days of s 95A(2).
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".

§ `Part 12 -- employee records (s 95)`

-- s 95(1): "An employer must make, and keep for the period prescribed (called in this section the record
-- retention period), employee records containing the prescribed particulars for (a) every employee the employer
-- employs; and (b) every former employee of the employer."
-- src:3810 | 95.—(1) An employer must make, and keep for the period
-- src:3811 | prescribed (called in this section the record retention period),
-- src:3812 | employee records containing the prescribed particulars for —
-- src:3814 | (a) every employee the employer employs; and
-- src:3816 | (b) every former employee of the employer.
@ref s 95(1) (src:3810-3816)
GIVEN `the person is an employee the employer employs or a former employee of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(1) the employer must make and keep an employee record for the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is an employee the employer employs or a former employee of the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "every employee the employer employs" and "every former employee of the employer"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 95(3): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1) if the employer makes or keeps an
-- employee record that is incomplete or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the record is
-- incomplete or inaccurate."
-- src:3831 | (3) An employer is taken to have failed to comply with
-- src:3832 | subsection (1) if the employer makes or keeps an employee record
-- src:3833 | that is incomplete or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew
-- src:3834 | that the record is incomplete or inaccurate.
@ref s 95(3) (src:3831-3834)
GIVEN `the employee record the employer makes or keeps is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(3) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the employee record the employer makes or keeps is incomplete or inaccurate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1) if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Seam S9.  The employer failed to comply with s 95(1) where the record was not made, was not kept for the
-- record retention period, did not contain the prescribed particulars, or is incomplete or inaccurate (s 95(3)).
-- src:3810 | 95.—(1) An employer must make, and keep for the period
-- src:3811 | prescribed (called in this section the record retention period),
-- src:3812 | employee records containing the prescribed particulars for —
-- src:3814 | (a) every employee the employer employs; and
-- src:3816 | (b) every former employee of the employer.
@ref s 95(1) (src:3810-3816)
-- src:3831 | (3) An employer is taken to have failed to comply with
-- src:3832 | subsection (1) if the employer makes or keeps an employee record
-- src:3833 | that is incomplete or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew
-- src:3834 | that the record is incomplete or inaccurate.
@ref s 95(3) (src:3831-3834)
GIVEN `the employer made the employee record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer kept the employee record for the record retention period prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee record contains the prescribed particulars` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee record the employer makes or keeps is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(1) the employer failed to comply` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the employer made the employee record`)
       OR (NOT `the employer kept the employee record for the record retention period prescribed`)
       OR (NOT `the employee record contains the prescribed particulars`)
       OR `s 95(3) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1)` `the employee record the employer makes or keeps is incomplete or inaccurate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Act says when the employer failed to comply and not when it complied
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 95(2): "An employer must ensure that an employee record made and kept under subsection (1) is, during the
-- record retention period prescribed for the employee record, readily accessible to the employee or former
-- employee to which the employee record relates."
-- src:3820 | (2) An employer must ensure that an employee record made and
-- src:3821 | kept under subsection (1) is, during the record retention period
-- src:3826 | prescribed for the employee record, readily accessible to the
-- src:3827 | employee or former employee to which the employee record relates.
@ref s 95(2) (src:3820-3827)
GIVEN `the employee record was readily accessible to the employee or former employee during the record retention period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(2) the employer failed to ensure that the employee record is readily accessible` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employee record was readily accessible to the employee or former employee during the record retention period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the employer must ensure and not when it has ensured it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 95(5): "'employee record', for an employee or a former employee of an employer, means a record of
-- information or particulars about the employment by the employer of the employee or former employee".
-- src:3844 | (5) In this section, “employee record”, for an employee or a former
-- src:3845 | employee of an employer, means a record of information or
-- src:3846 | particulars about the employment by the employer of the employee
-- src:3847 | or former employee, as the case may be.
@ref s 95(5) (src:3844-3847)
GIVEN `the record is a record of information or particulars about the employment by the employer of the employee or former employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95(5) "employee record" the record is one` MEANS
    IF `the record is a record of information or particulars about the employment by the employer of the employee or former employee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a record of information or particulars about the employment by the employer of the employee"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Part 12 -- the written record of key employment terms (s 95A)`

-- s 95A(1): "This section only applies to, and in relation to, every employee (a) who enters into a contract of
-- service with the employer on or after 1 April 2016; and (b) who is employed under that contract for a period
-- not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service."
-- src:3853 | 95A.—(1) This section only applies to, and in relation to, every
-- src:3854 | employee —
-- src:3856 | (a) who enters into a contract of service with the employer on
-- src:3857 | or after 1 April 2016; and
-- src:3859 | (b) who is employed under that contract for a period not
-- src:3860 | shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service.
@ref s 95A(1) (src:3853-3860)
GIVEN `the day the employee entered into the contract of service` IS A DATE
      `the employee is employed under the contract for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(1) section 95A applies to the employee` MEANS
    IF `the day the employee entered into the contract of service` AT LEAST (Date 1 4 2016)
       AND `the employee is employed under the contract for a period not shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section only applies to, and in relation to, every employee"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 95A(2): "An employer must give each employee of the employer a written record of the key employment terms of
-- the employee not later than 14 days after the day that the employee starts employment with the employer, or
-- within such other period as may be prescribed in substitution."  "14 days after the day" is counted as the
-- Interpretation Act counts "from" and s 50(b) is applied to the last day (fork F15: that Act counts only "from").
-- src:3864 | (2) An employer must give each employee of the employer a
-- src:3865 | written record of the key employment terms of the employee not later
-- src:3866 | than 14 days after the day that the employee starts employment with
-- src:3867 | the employer, or within such other period as may be prescribed in
-- src:3868 | substitution.
@ref s 95A(2) (src:3864-3868)
GIVEN `the day the employee starts employment` IS A DATE
      `the number of days prescribed in substitution` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 95A(2) the last day for giving the written record of the key employment terms` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of days prescribed in substitution`
    WHEN JUST days THEN
        `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the day the employee starts employment` PLUS days) Days `the public holidays` `a contrary intention appears`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `the last day of the period once section 50(b) is applied` (`the day the employee starts employment` PLUS 14) Days `the public holidays` `a contrary intention appears`

-- s 95A(5): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (2) if the written record given is
-- incomplete or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the record is incomplete or inaccurate."
-- src:3901 | (5) An employer is taken to have failed to comply with
-- src:3902 | subsection (2) if the written record given is incomplete or
-- src:3903 | inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the record is
-- src:3904 | incomplete or inaccurate.
@ref s 95A(5) (src:3901-3904)
GIVEN `the written record given is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(5) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the written record given is incomplete or inaccurate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (2) if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Seam S10.  The employer failed to comply with s 95A(2) where section 95A applies and no exemption by order under
-- subsection (6) is given, and either the record given is incomplete or inaccurate (s 95A(5)), or it was given after the
-- last day, or none was given and the last day has passed.
-- src:3853 | 95A.—(1) This section only applies to, and in relation to, every
-- src:3854 | employee —
-- src:3856 | (a) who enters into a contract of service with the employer on
-- src:3857 | or after 1 April 2016; and
-- src:3859 | (b) who is employed under that contract for a period not
-- src:3860 | shorter than the prescribed minimum period of service.
-- src:3864 | (2) An employer must give each employee of the employer a
-- src:3865 | written record of the key employment terms of the employee not later
-- src:3866 | than 14 days after the day that the employee starts employment with
-- src:3867 | the employer, or within such other period as may be prescribed in
-- src:3868 | substitution.
@ref s 95A(2) (src:3853-3868)
-- src:3901 | (5) An employer is taken to have failed to comply with
-- src:3902 | subsection (2) if the written record given is incomplete or
-- src:3903 | inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the record is
-- src:3904 | incomplete or inaccurate.
@ref s 95A(5) (src:3901-3904)
GIVEN `the answer of s 95A(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the employer from the provision in respect of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day for giving the written record` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the written record was given` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the written record given is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the question is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(2) the employer failed to comply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 95A "only applies to" the employee described in subsection (1)
        IF `the answer of s 95A(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 95A applies to the employee is the answer of s 95A(1), which was not given
        IF `the answer of s 95A(1)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister may exempt by order under subsection (6)
        IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the employer from the provision in respect of the employee` THEN NOTHING
        IF `s 95A(5) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (2)` `the written record given is incomplete or inaccurate` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF CONSIDER `the last day for giving the written record`
           WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
           WHEN JUST last THEN
               CONSIDER `the day the written record was given`
               WHEN JUST given THEN given GREATER THAN last
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the question is asked about` GREATER THAN last
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Act says when the employer failed to comply and not when it complied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- s 95A(3): "The requirement to give a written record of key employment terms to an employee in subsection (2)
-- is satisfied if (a) an electronic record containing the key employment terms is provided in a manner that
-- enables the information contained in the electronic record to be accessible and useable by the employee for
-- subsequent reference; or (b) the key employment terms are published on an Internet website (i) which is
-- authorised by the employer and readily accessible to the employee; and (ii) which address is disseminated by
-- the employer to the employee."  Subsection (4) says (3) does not limit any other manner, so a failure to
-- meet (3) is not a "no".
-- src:3872 | (3) The requirement to give a written record of key employment
-- src:3873 | terms to an employee in subsection (2) is satisfied if —
-- src:3875 | (a) an electronic record containing the key employment terms
-- src:3876 | is provided in a manner that enables the information
-- src:3881 | contained in the electronic record to be accessible and
-- src:3882 | useable by the employee for subsequent reference; or
-- src:3884 | (b) the key employment terms are published on an Internet
-- src:3885 | website —
-- src:3887 | (i) which is authorised by the employer and readily
-- src:3888 | accessible to the employee; and
-- src:3890 | (ii) which address is disseminated by the employer to the
-- src:3891 | employee.
@ref s 95A(3) (src:3872-3891)
GIVEN `an electronic record containing the key employment terms was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by the employee for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the key employment terms are published on an Internet website authorised by the employer and readily accessible to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address of that website was disseminated by the employer to the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(3) the requirement to give a written record is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `an electronic record containing the key employment terms was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by the employee for subsequent reference`
       OR (`the key employment terms are published on an Internet website authorised by the employer and readily accessible to the employee`
           AND `the address of that website was disseminated by the employer to the employee`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) says that subsection (3) does not limit any other manner of giving a written record
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 95A(4): "To avoid doubt, subsection (3) does not limit any other manner of giving to an employee a written
-- record of the key employment terms of the employee."
-- src:3895 | (4) To avoid doubt, subsection (3) does not limit any other manner
-- src:3896 | of giving to an employee a written record of the key employment
-- src:3897 | terms of the employee.
@ref s 95A(4) (src:3895-3897)
GIVEN `the record was given in some manner other than those in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(4) subsection (3) limits the manner of giving the record` MEANS
    IF `the record was given in some manner other than those in subsection (3)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (3) does not limit any other manner of giving to an employee a written"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of another manner of giving the record
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 95A(7): "'key employment term', for an employee, means any type of term of employment contained in a contract
-- of service between an employer and the employee that is prescribed to be a key employment term."
-- src:3920 | (7) In this section, “key employment term”, for an employee, means
-- src:3921 | any type of term of employment contained in a contract of service
-- src:3922 | between an employer and the employee that is prescribed to be a key
-- src:3923 | employment term.
@ref s 95A(7) (src:3920-3923)
GIVEN `the type of term is contained in the contract of service and is prescribed to be a key employment term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(7) "key employment term" the term is one` MEANS
    IF `the type of term is contained in the contract of service and is prescribed to be a key employment term`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any type of term of employment contained in a contract of service"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§ `Part 12 -- pay slips (s 96)`

-- s 96(1)(a): "Subject to subsection (2), an employer must give to every employee of the employer a pay slip,
-- within the time prescribed for giving pay slips, for all salary paid by the employer for the salary period or
-- salary periods to which the pay slip relates".
-- src:3932 | 96.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), an employer must give —
-- src:3934 | (a) to every employee of the employer a pay slip, within the
-- src:3935 | time prescribed for giving pay slips, for all salary paid by
-- src:3936 | the employer for the salary period or salary periods to
-- src:3937 | which the pay slip relates; and
@ref s 96(1)(a) (src:3932-3937)
GIVEN `the employer paid salary for the salary period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer gave the employee the pay slip within the time prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1)(a) the employer failed to give the employee a pay slip` MEANS
    IF `the employer paid salary for the salary period` AND (NOT `the employer gave the employee the pay slip within the time prescribed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the employer must give and not when it has given it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 96(1)(b): "to every employee a pay slip for every sum paid by the employer under section 22 or 23."
-- src:3939 | (b) to every employee a pay slip for every sum paid by the
-- src:3940 | employer under section 22 or 23.
@ref s 96(1)(b) (src:3939-3940)
GIVEN `the employer paid a sum under section 22 or 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer gave the employee a pay slip for that sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1)(b) the employer failed to give the employee a pay slip for the sum paid` MEANS
    IF `the employer paid a sum under section 22 or 23` AND (NOT `the employer gave the employee a pay slip for that sum`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says what the employer must give and not when it has given it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 96(4): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1) if the pay slip given to an
-- employee is incomplete or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the pay slip is incomplete or inaccurate."
-- src:3958 | (4) An employer is taken to have failed to comply with
-- src:3959 | subsection (1) if the pay slip given to an employee is incomplete
-- src:3960 | or inaccurate, whether or not the employer knew that the pay slip is
-- src:3961 | incomplete or inaccurate.
@ref s 96(4) (src:3958-3961)
GIVEN `the pay slip given to the employee is incomplete or inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(4) the employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the pay slip given to the employee is incomplete or inaccurate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employer is taken to have failed to comply with subsection (1) if"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 96(2): "A pay slip given by an employer to an employee must be in the form prescribed (if prescribed) and
-- must contain all the information prescribed."
-- src:3944 | (2) A pay slip given by an employer to an employee must be in the
-- src:3945 | form prescribed (if prescribed) and must contain all the information
-- src:3946 | prescribed.
@ref s 96(2) (src:3944-3946)
GIVEN `the pay slip is in the form prescribed, if a form is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pay slip contains all the information prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(2) the pay slip given meets the requirements of form and information` MEANS
    IF `the pay slip is in the form prescribed, if a form is prescribed` AND `the pay slip contains all the information prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says what the pay slip must be and contain and not the consequence of a pay slip that is not
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 96(3): "The requirement to give a pay slip to an employee under this section is satisfied if an electronic
-- record containing the prescribed information of a pay slip is provided in a manner that enables the information
-- contained in the electronic record to be accessible and useable by the employee for subsequent reference."
-- src:3950 | (3) The requirement to give a pay slip to an employee under this
-- src:3951 | section is satisfied if an electronic record containing the prescribed
-- src:3952 | information of a pay slip is provided in a manner that enables the
-- src:3953 | information contained in the electronic record to be accessible and
-- src:3954 | useable by the employee for subsequent reference.
@ref s 96(3) (src:3950-3954)
GIVEN `an electronic record containing the prescribed information of a pay slip was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by the employee for subsequent reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(3) the requirement to give a pay slip is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `an electronic record containing the prescribed information of a pay slip was provided in a manner that makes it accessible and useable by the employee for subsequent reference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says one way in which the requirement is satisfied and does not say that no other way satisfies it
    ELSE NOTHING

