      `the answer of s 96(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the employer from the provision in respect of the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) the employer failed to comply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Minister may exempt by order under subsection (5)
        IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the employer from the provision in respect of the employee` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the answer of s 96(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 96(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of s 96(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
